from lb import e
E=[
e("Book 10 - Summary (Cardinas, the Death Pact, Undeath, Gary the Demigod)",["Book 10","Cardinas","Citadel of Pillars","natural array","Death Pact","Keeper of the Cycle","Cup of Heroes","Undeath avatar","Divine Ghost Fire","elemental messengers"],
"""BOOK 10 (Yaresh region, Pallimustus; autumn-winter after Book 9): In the aftermath of Yaresh, Jason hides messenger defectors (Marek, Tera, Jali) in his astral realm, bargains with Allayeth (diamond) and Charist, shames the Aristocratic Faction with Continental Council envoy Marcus Hargrave Xenoria, and recruits the Church of Liberty. Jason gets Colin hatched as his Voice of the Will. Kaal hands over a messenger device (a dimensional differentiator to forge a soul forge) and Jason leads a silver/gold expedition (Team Biscuit, Rick Geller's team, Korinne's team, Team Moon's Edge, Emir, Gabriel, Arabelle, Amos, Carlos, Hana) down the shaft into the natural array: elemental messengers, spider moles, the Cult of the Builder (Beaufort), the brightheart Smoulder city Cardinas (Citadel of Pillars; Lorenn, Marla) and the corrupted Birthing Tree. Destruction and the Church of Undeath (Garth Larosse, Jameela, Jeff) turn ~200,000 dead into undead. Jason prays to the goddess of Death and makes the Death Pact: he can never resurrect himself or others; title Keeper of the Cycle; Divine Ghost Fire. Boris Ket Lundi (an Earth-born Unorthodox messenger) joins. Gary drinks the Cup of Heroes to become a demigod and holds the wall. The tree and shaft are prepared for a transformation zone, ending with Jason's ritual starting the zone. Appendix lists Jason's silver abilities.""",10),
e("Death Pact and Keeper of the Cycle",["Death Pact","Keeper of the Cycle","Sanctity of Death","goddess of Death","Divine Ghost Fire","ghost fire"],
"""In the Cardinas death chamber Jason prays and meets the goddess of Death (a stocky middle-aged woman in a colourful dress in this region; 'Death knows how to wait'). She refuses his banked resurrections as sacrifice and offers a pact: Jason may never resurrect himself or anyone else (he may stasis the dying until another resurrects). In return: title Keeper of the Cycle; undeath energy is excluded from his soul realm, spirit domains and aura; divine power given to undead is negated; afflictions also apply Ghost Fire (harmless to living, calms and shields from undeath; transcendent DoT on undead); allies in his aura gain ghost fire. Death's miracle is Divine Ghost Fire on all defenders (white ethereal flames; may not resurrect while under it; spreads to undead) and resetting Undeath's claimed territory once. Jason hands over his stored messenger life-force. In Book 12 Death later returns the stored resurrection power (it can no longer be misused) but the pact still bars him from resurrecting others.""",10),
e("Church of Undeath and Garth Larosse",["Undeath","Church of Undeath","Garth Larosse","Jameela","Priest Jeff","Undeath avatar","boomers","spawning pits"],
"""God Undeath (a living man in black robes with crimson-spark eyes and gravel voice) is the corruption of the cycle itself; his church is reviled. In Cardinas his priests turn ~200,000 dead brighthearts and messengers into undead (spawning pits, 'boomer' exploding mounds, grave and pyre elementals). High Priest Garth Larosse (9 ft lich-like skeleton from a dozen monsters, green cloak, red-eyed skull, 'Skeletor'/chuuni) leads dozens of gold/silver priests; Priestess Jameela (tall, beautiful ex-adventurer); silver Priest Jeff (comic relief; grandmother a high priestess of Destruction). They try to build an avatar of Undeath (giant zombie) from the best corpse parts using the messenger tree as base. Undeath says 'the enemy has one with the power. Jason Asano; kill him if you can.' Later (Book 11) Garth is killed via an incompatible messenger heart. Destruction 'gleefully stepped back to watch'.""",10),
e("Cardinas and the Brighthearts",["Cardinas","Brightheart","brightheart smoulder","Citadel of Pillars","Lorenn","Marla","Hilda","Kollas","growth chambers","echo array"],
"""Cardinas: underground Smoulder city ruled from the Citadel of Pillars, a dimensional prefabrication of clashing architecture, population under 10,000 survivors (less than 1/20). Brightheart Smoulder have obsidian skin with glowing affinity markings (fire, ash, magma, metal). Last council member Lorenn (ash aspect); guide Marla (metal, red-orange glow, gay); Hilda (young magma silver); Kollas (metal-shaper defender). Their ancestors came by a long tunnel from the west; they were peaceful and elementals were placid. The natural array's wellspring: three balancing essences at its heart (plant, life, water). The Builder cult (led by Beaufort, an elf-disguised 15 ft girder-skeleton war form) invaded to take Cardinas's uniquely solid astral space; messengers punched in and left a Birthing Tree. Jason evacuates ~10,000 brighthearts into his soul realm (they later found Rexion/Outer Rexion).""",10),
e("Birthing Tree and Soul Forge attempt",["Birthing Tree","corrupted birthing tree","tree pillar volcano","dimensional differentiator","soul forge attempt"],
"""The messengers' device is a dimensional differentiator that isolates elemental layers of the natural array to create a neutral matrix (a soul forge, every astral king having one except Jason). The Birthing Tree in the natural array chamber (leafless pillar-volcano, lava sap) is the corrupted result of a failed attempt to create a soul forge; its roots consume organic matter and spawn elemental messengers; its will is young, scared and erratic, not malevolent. Jason resolves to heal it; later the tree person becomes Arbour/Voice of the Will in Jason's soul (Book 11).""",10),
e("Beaufort (Builder cult gold-ranker)",["Beaufort","Beaufort Builder cult","the Defier Beaufort"],
"""Beaufort: gold-ranker head of the Builder-cult forces in Cardinas; elf body is a disguise, true war form a 15 ft girder skeleton of dark iron with four arms, harpoon trident and ceramic axe; star seed gives internal dimensional storage; no essences. Calls Jason 'the Defier'. The Builder urged him to bet on Jason's mercy. They ally in Book 10.""",10),
e("Allayeth and Charist",["Allayeth","Charist","Ally","diamond elves"],
"""Allayeth: diamond elf (green eyes, light-brown skin, wavy wood-brown hair), last of her family; subtle diplomat; mentor of Team Moon's Edge; childhood trauma (fleeing a burning home); enters Jason's soul realm and learns the power is Jason himself; asks him to call her 'Ally'; fears 'a planet won't hold you'; killed all messenger servants with thorns in Ch45 ('Some things can't be forgiven'). Charist: blunt, confrontational diamond elf of Yaresh; breaks into Jason's palace; flings elemental messengers at the moon with an air vortex. Both settled in Yaresh and limit themselves to the region.""",10),
e("Team Moon's Edge and Miriam Vance",["Team Moon's Edge","Miriam Vance","Valetta","Alice berserker","Moon's Edge"],
"""Team Moon's Edge: six all-woman gold-rank team mentored by Allayeth; tactical commander Miriam Vance; Valetta (floats in silver light, architect, watches rather than rescues researchers to test Jason, later given a second chance); Alice (berserker 'zone of annihilation'). Miriam questions Jason and works the death-chamber defence.""",10),
e("Continental Council envoy Marcus Hargrave Xenoria",["Marcus Xenoria","Marcus Hargrave Xenoria","Gormanston Bynes","Aristocratic Faction","Calcifer Bynes","Musin Heath"],
"""Marcus Hargrave Xenoria: huge snow-white leonid gold-ranker in biker leather (Unquenchable flame; advised by Danielle Geller), Continental Council envoy; strips sinecure Adventure Society memberships in Yaresh, extends monster-surge policy. The Aristocratic Faction (merchant barons and old money; led by Gormanston Bynes, core-free gold fortress-like; niece Juniper Bynes, silver; Calcifer Bynes director of External Affairs) runs Yaresh; Gormanston wants to 'drydock and burn the ship'. AS director Musin Heath (elf, gold core user) supports Jason. Lord Warthington-Hampstead (Magic Society) tries to seize Schaat's orb; Humphrey humiliates him.""",10),
e("Council of Kings",["Council of Kings","Jamis Fran Muskar","Erigo Fin Desca","Vesta Carmis Zell","prime avatar Jamis","originals astral kings"],
"""Council of Kings (Book 10 Ch15): a meeting of astral kings aboard a dimension ship near a dying universe, where the Builder's world engineers wrap a lush green-blue planet in intrinsic-mandate magic to move it to a fresh universe as payment to astral kings. Participants: Jamis Fran Muskar (prime avatar of an astral king; hedonistic 7-ft celestine-like with dark copper hair; says Jason is no threat and calls astral kings who aren't messengers 'originals'), Vesta Carmis Zell (Yaresh king; wants a second soul forge and Jason dead after use), the new Builder's prime vessel Erigo Fin Desca (ex-messenger and ex-Unorthodoxy; silver metal wings, amber glass eyes). Purification artefact is the council's goal. Zithis Carrow Vayel is the Builder's name.""",10),
e("Colin - Voice of the Will",["Colin Voice of the Will","Colin four forms","Apocalypse Beast Colin","Worm That Walks Colin","nascent astral hegemon"],
"""Colin hatches in Book 10 as Jason's Voice of the Will (a bonded avatar): four forms - Swarm (more biomass and hive range), The Worm That Walks (rags/leather straps entangle), Apocalypse Beast (headless four-armed mouth-covered blood giant ~2x Humphrey, later 8-armed eye-mouthed sphere; feeding seals enemy powers) and Voice of the Will (looks exactly like Jason with red-ember eyes in a void; Jason-level intellect; uses most of Jason's abilities except astral-hegemon ones; influence over branded messengers). The system calls Jason a 'Nascent Astral Hegemon' (variant astral king). Colin's cocoon in the astral kingdom is a glass sphere. Stash welcomes him.""",10),
e("Jali Corrik Fen",["Jali","Jali Corrik Fen","Jali messenger"],
"""Jali Corrik Fen: perpetual-silver female messenger (born at the limit), expendable envoy who delivers the messenger device; has quietly shed indoctrination; her astral king notices and tries to kill her (gestalt tears itself) but Jason shields her with astral-gate authority; she enters his realm, remakes her inner torture castle into a cenote garden, erases her brand by sitting on the throne herself and flies. Gary hostilely puts her to work cleaning his smithy. She is one of the freed newborn messengers in Book 11 era.""",10),
e("Tera, Marek and the Unorthodoxy in Jason's realm",["Tera Jun Casta soul realm","Marek soul realm","Mari Gah Rahnd","messenger asylum"],
"""Tera wakes in Jason's astral kingdom with her brand and silver cap gone and flees in horror; Marek (Unorthodoxy) explains. Jason remoulded misbehaving messengers' bodies (Mari Gah Rahnd lost mouth/arms/legs/wings for days). Marek's people have a Soviet-concrete-block inner world; Jali a fairy-tale castle; Jason offers freed messengers the choice of release into the cosmos via the goddess Liberty's priestess Raelia Cass.""",10),
e("Boris Ket Lundi (Ketland)",["Boris Ket Lundi","Boris Ketland","Boris messenger","Unorthodoxy Boris","Cabal founder Boris"],
"""Boris Ket Lundi (Boris Ketland): gold-rank messenger of the Unorthodoxy, from Earth (spent far more time on Earth than Jason; a founder and global leader of the Cabal, posing as a Cabal/government counterpart of Darius and Michael); sold by his true astral king to Vesta Carmis Zell to ensure Jason succeeds; a block holds his brand ~12 days; claims best astral-magic specialist on the planet (Jason second) and 'best lover in the cosmos'. Gabriel Remore rescues him from the death-chamber gate. In Book 11-12 he helps with Earth, vampire war, and the Slovakian meeting.""",10),
e("Gary's Cup of Heroes (Book 10)",["Cup of Heroes","Gary demigod","Gary hero","Gary Divine Forge","Gary's Divine Armour","Gary giant"],
"""On the fifth floor of the Cardinas death-chamber wall the god Hero (leonid-aspect, gentle voice, calls Gary 'Gareth') offers the Cup of Heroes; Gary has 7h41m for his soul to contain the power. His body becomes a gestalt: Hammer -> Divine Hammer, Fire -> Divine Fire, Iron -> Divine Iron, Forge confluence -> Demigod essence. Abilities: All-Seeing Eye, First Son of the Leonids, Vessel of the Ancestors (grow to giant size), Divine Forge, Hero (aura: all attributes up, cooldown reset, DR, resist, cleanse, regen, divine protection). He rises from gold 0 through gold 9 to diamond 0, golden eyes, forges Divine Armour, six Large Hammers and Gary's Last Hammer, and fights the avatar of Undeath kaiju-style. It is irreversible ('doesn't come back from the dead'); sacrifice was his choice; in Book 11 he dies ~1 year later.""",10),
e("Hero and Genesis Command: Source",["Hero god","Genesis Command Source","Hero's miracle","Hero Jason three times"],
"""Hero (god; appears human in plain armour): his influence is by role/mandate; his miracle is offered to heroes at their darkest moment; three times Jason met the conditions. Hero gives Jason [Genesis Command: Source] (transcendent legendary, 1/1): assign or reassign a source of power - like the Healer's Genesis Command: Life. Hero's power returns to him after Gary's death unless reassigned (Jason's hint that 'this time the one who gets the choice is you'). Hero on Purity: a human-dominant empire's 'purity' war led to the Order before Disguise took over.""",10),
e("Gods meeting Jason: Knowledge, Destruction, Dominion",["Destruction god","Knowledge appears Jason","Dominion voice","gods can't affect Jason"],
"""Destruction (rumbling avalanche voice) takes over priests holding a messenger beacon and kills them. Knowledge (bookish woman in brown robes) advises that Jason can trigger a zone again as sacred ground; says Beaufort's intentions are honest. Dominion interrupts a meeting ('Sod off'). Jason is unaffected by the general divine will of gods (the nascent astral king excised him from their power over mortals of that world); gods can still affect him in their own sphere.""",10),
e("Mah Go Schaat's study",["Schaat's study","Mango Shot","aura keystone","study orb"],
"""Mah Go Schaat's study (orb the size of a small cottage atop a stronghold tower) is delivered to Jason via a convoy; a keystone from Schaat's body (imbued with astral-king ambitions) opens it; inside only research, no relics: astral-magic secrets for finishing the dimensional bridge. Marek warns all diamond-rankers self-resurrect (Schaat will return). Allayeth impales the messenger servants who delivered it.""",10),
e("Jason's Fate Senses (Quest System)",["fate senses","Eyes of the Crucible","Destiny magic","intrinsic-mandate magic","Quest System fate"],
"""Shade explains fate senses (Eyes of the Crucible, Way of the Crossroads): unconscious senses of important events; conditions: near-inert low-rank soul, malleable state (yanked through astral), close encounter with a maximally powerful force. Jason's Quest System was his fate sense; it evolved into sensing Gordon's potential for intrinsic-mandate magic (high-order magic of transcendent entities that shapes reality: the Builder forging worlds; World-Phoenix hardening Earth's barrier). The World-Phoenix token was intended to instil fate senses; not everyone survives.""",10),
e("Taika, Fertility church and Church of Liberty (Book 10)",["Hennith","Fertility priestess","Raelia Cass","Church of Liberty","Liberty goddess"],
"""Fertility priestess Hennith (acolytes Fennick and Cassa) wants samples for a breeding programme (anti-messenger forces); Taika flees ('creepy eugenics'). Priestess Raelia Cass (human, silver, Church of Liberty) works with Allayeth: Liberty approves freeing messengers but they must be released into the cosmos; Liberty will hide Jason's actions from Knowledge. Liberty is antagonistic to Dominion.""",10),
e("Amalgeth",["Amalgeth","fungal monster Amalgeth"],
"""Amalgeth: intelligent shape-shifting fungal monster that infiltrates isolated communities, learns, and slowly escalates predation timed with monster activity; killed people become mutable flesh; exposed it rampages, spawns a fully grown copy with memories and triggers accelerated plant growth. Starts at silver, advances to gold with reproduction. Allayeth killed one.""",10),
e("Thadwick the Energy Vampire in Jorganis",["Thadwick energy vampire","Jorganis","Purity relic Thadwick","sword to kill messengers"],
"""Thadwick (now an energy vampire, former Thadwick Mercer) leads a vampire coterie in Jorganis (lawless island city, Pacific-equivalent) where messengers have moved in; he killed a gold messenger with the black-and-red messenger-killing sword (sealed by the Builder; he devoured the soul containing it) and asks about the Purity relic.""",10),
e("Jason's soul realm tour",["soul realm tour","rose garden","blood garden","Flesh Pit","soul realm regions"],
"""Jason's soul realm by essence: rose garden (blood; smells of immortality), underground mushroom caverns (dark), rope-bridge gorge with mana creeks, farmhouse where Tera perches, vampire-manor estate (dark+blood; man-eating hedges, clocks with old symbols), the Flesh Pit (recreated sacrifice chamber), the Colin greenhouse, library avatars, a door sign 'The Astral Gate Containment Centre and Standish Family Adult Recreation Retrospective'. Mana flows in creeks; the Builder's flaying taught him soul attacks. He can stabilise any physical reality he is inside.""",10),
e("The Rexion hold-outs: Gary and Farrah (Book 10)",["Farrah Voice of the Will","Farrah nascent","Farrah resurrected by Reaper request"],
"""Farrah was resurrected by the Reaper at the World-Phoenix's request because the World-Phoenix feared Jason would let Earth die. Her status shows 'Voice of the Will (Nascent)'. She leads array knowledge; Farrah says Earth's grid is an artificial array using natural-array principles at planetary scale, probably developed by messengers.""",10),
e("Storm Kingdom royals: Zara in Book 10",["Zara copper hair","Zara Nareen Book 10","Zara forgiveness"],
"""Zara (copper hair cut short after Jason ordered her to change it) apologises for the mess in Rimaros; Jason says he is 'trying out forgiveness as a philosophy'. They share half-flirtations (Ch88). Zara refinances Yaresh debts for Jason (including Bellory's) using House Nareen.""",10),
e("Jason's relationship attitude and Earth guilt",["Jason Gerling revenge","Kaito Asya Greg Book 10","Jason Earth killings"],
"""Jason says on Earth he publicly executed people (family grew reticent; Ian is a doctor he hoped to bring); lover, brother and friend were killed. His rage returns when he learns Gary drank the Cup of Heroes; Farrah scolds him; Rufus: 'Is that what it feels like every time I—' 'Yes.'""",10),
e("Genesis Command: Life requires a Soul Forge",["Genesis Command Life soul forge","Healer gift soul forge"],
"""Healer's [Genesis Command: Life] says 'You do not meet the qualifications to activate this device in the current space. Missing element: soul forge.' So Jason's realm lacks a soul forge until Book 11's reintegration.""",10),
e("Jason's Silver 5 ability states (Book 10)",["Jason silver 5","Punish silver 5","Silver 5"],
"""Book 10: Punish Silver 5 42%; Verdict, Feast of Absolution, Hegemony etc. at Silver 4-5; Appendix I lists silver abilities: Dark - Midnight Eyes, Hand of the Reaper (numerous arms), Cloak of Night (flight, space distortion), Path of Shadows (continental portals), Shadow familiar (31 bodies); Blood - Blood Harvest, Leech Bite (Tainted Meridians), Haemorrhage (Blood From a Stone), Feast of Blood, Sanguine Horror; Sin - Punish (Penance), Castigate (Mortality), Feast of Absolution (wide area), Sin Eater (exceed baseline), Hegemony (downgrades transcendent damage); Doom - Inexorable Doom (Persecution), Doom Blade (sword, Price in Blood), Punition (mana tiers), Verdict (Sanction), Avatar of Doom (Harbinger).""",10),
]
